From 9f011576786d06d6f07940ee9833614d235f5286 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:15:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: give SSRF-guard and PM-build tests offline resolvers
 and toolchains [daveey]

With the loopback-only fence, tests whose code under test resolves a URL's host
itself (url_safety, browser CDP/eval guards, Slack file URLs, web extract) saw a
refusal and failed closed. They now request the opt-in public_dns fixture:
IP literals resolve numerically, localhost through the real resolver, other
names to a fixed public address; nothing is dialled. PM build tests pin the
host uv/interpreter instead of downloading python-build-standalone, and the
subdirectory plugin update test publishes through admission_env. Real pypi.org
canaries in the plugin sandbox suite are marked live, and the live marker text
now says it is the fence's only opt-out.
